<main class="page">
  <div class="content">
    <a href="/blog" class="back">← Back to Blog</a>
    
    <h1>Pulse v0.7.0: The Islands Architecture</h1>
    <span class="date">January 20, 2025</span>
    
    <div class="body">
      <p class="lead">With release v0.7, Pulse introduces its signature <strong>Islands Architecture</strong>. This paradigm shift allows you to ship interactive components into mostly static HTML pages without hydration penalties.</p>
      
      <h3>🏝️ Partial Hydration</h3>
      <p>Traditional SPAs hydrate the entire page, costing precious milliseconds of Main Thread time. Pulse v0.7 flips this. By default, everything is static HTML. You explicitly opt-in to interactivity using our reactive components. The framework sends 0KB of JavaScript for static content, and only loads independent "islands" of interactivity where needed.</p>

      <h3>🔄 Primitives: List & Show</h3>
      <p>We introduced the core control flow primitives: <code>&lt;List&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;Show&gt;</code>. Unlike other frameworks that use compiler magic around `.map()`, Pulse primitives are optimized at the compiler level to handle DOM updates efficiently. This reduces the boilerplate needed for rendering collections and conditional logic.</p>

      <h3>💅 Smart Scoped CSS</h3>
      <p>v0.7 brings automatic CSS scoping. Styles defined in a <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> block are hashed and attached locally to the component. No more naming collisions or BEM methodology requirements—just write <code is:raw>.button {}</code> and let Pulse handle the rest.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

